{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ADPcvvX9BqtFRac1XAZqNP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(Saved from LinkedIn as text, October 2026)\n2\t\n3\tInes Okafor\n4\tHead Chef at Saltmarsh. Fermentation, whole-vegetable cooking, apprentices.\n5\tLeeds, England, United Kingdom\n6\t\n7\tABOUT\n8\tI cook at Saltmarsh, a 40-seat restaurant in Leeds. Most of what I care about\n9\thappens before service: what we do with the trim, the whey, the stems and the\n10\tbones. We have a wall of jars and a prep list that is longer than the menu.\n11\tI run our apprentice programme and write a small zine about preserving,\n12\tcalled Brine.\n13\t\n14\tEXPERIENCE\n15\t\n16\tHead Chef, Saltmarsh, Leeds\n17\tMar 2022 to present\n18\t- A menu that changes every week\n19\t- Cut kitchen food waste from 14 kg to 5 kg a week\n20\t- Built the larder: 40+ ferments, vinegars and garums on rotation\n21\t- Two apprentices a year since 2023\n22\t\n23\tSous Chef, The Corn Exchange Kitchen, Leeds\n24\tJun 2019 to Feb 2022\n25\t- Ran the pass on a 90-cover service\n26\t- Took over ordering and brought the supplier list from 31 to 12\n27\t\n28\tChef de Partie, Brassica, Manchester\n29\tSep 2016 to May 2019\n30\t- Larder and garnish, then sauce\n31\t\n32\tFjaerland Fermentation Lab, Norway\n33\tJan 2018 to Mar 2018\n34\t\n35\tEDUCATION\n36\tLeeds Kitchen College. Diploma in Professional Cookery, 2014 to 2016\n37\t\n38\tVOLUNTEERING\n39\tSunday Pot, Leeds. Co-founder. 2021 to present\n40\tA hot meal every Sunday at St Aidan's hall, cooked from what restaurants in\n41\tthe city have left over.\n42\t\n43\tPUBLICATIONS\n44\tBrine. A zine about preserving. Four issues, 2022 to 2025.\n45\t\n46\tRECOMMENDATIONS\n47\tCallum Reyes, owner of Saltmarsh:\n48\t\"Ines turned our bins into a larder. The best thing on the menu most weeks\n49\tstarted as something we used to throw away.\"\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2d15a00-3735-4dcc-b3b9-bc51cda185ae","uuid":"c0096c38-0899-4bd8-a291-644a1f3ea129","timestamp":"2026-10-10T04:46:53.654Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"material/linkedin.md","content":"(Saved from LinkedIn as text, October 2026)\n\nInes Okafor\nHead Chef at Saltmarsh. Fermentation, whole-vegetable cooking, apprentices.\nLeeds, England, United Kingdom\n\nABOUT\nI cook at Saltmarsh, a 40-seat restaurant in Leeds. Most of what I care about\nhappens before service: what we do with the trim, the whey, the stems and the\nbones. We have a wall of jars and a prep list that is longer than the menu.\nI run our apprentice programme and write a small zine about preserving,\ncalled Brine.\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nHead Chef, Saltmarsh, Leeds\nMar 2022 to present\n- A menu that changes every week\n- Cut kitchen food waste from 14 kg to 5 kg a week\n- Built the larder: 40+ ferments, vinegars and garums on rotation\n- Two apprentices a year since 2023\n\nSous Chef, The Corn Exchange Kitchen, Leeds\nJun 2019 to Feb 2022\n- Ran the pass on a 90-cover service\n- Took over ordering and brought the supplier list from 31 to 12\n\nChef de Partie, Brassica, Manchester\nSep 2016 to May 2019\n- Larder and garnish, then sauce\n\nFjaerland Fermentation Lab, Norway\nJan 2018 to Mar 2018\n\nEDUCATION\nLeeds Kitchen College. Diploma in Professional Cookery, 2014 to 2016\n\nVOLUNTEERING\nSunday Pot, Leeds. Co-founder. 2021 to present\nA hot meal every Sunday at St Aidan's hall, cooked from what restaurants in\nthe city have left over.\n\nPUBLICATIONS\nBrine. A zine about preserving. Four issues, 2022 to 2025.\n\nRECOMMENDATIONS\nCallum Reyes, owner of Saltmarsh:\n\"Ines turned our bins into a larder. The best thing on the menu most weeks\nstarted as something we used to throw away.\"\n","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":50}}}
